### list all projects
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/projects/

### create a project
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/projects/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=abc

--abc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

BookNest - Online Library Management System
--abc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

<h2>BookNest - Online Library Management System</h2>

<p>
BookNest is a comprehensive Django-based Online Library Management System designed
to streamline book catalog management, member registration, borrowing workflows,
reservations, and reporting. The platform provides role-based access for administrators,
librarians, and members, enabling efficient library operations through a modern
web interface and RESTful APIs.
</p>

<h3>Key Features</h3>
<ul>
    <li>User Authentication & Authorization</li>
    <li>Book and Category Management</li>
    <li>ISBN Tracking and Inventory Control</li>
    <li>Borrow and Return Management</li>
    <li>Book Reservation System</li>
    <li>Advanced Search & Filtering</li>
    <li>User Reviews and Ratings</li>
    <li>Admin Dashboard with Analytics</li>
    <li>Django REST Framework API Support</li>
    <li>CKEditor-based Content Management</li>
</ul>

<h3>Technology Stack</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Django</li>
    <li>Django REST Framework</li>
    <li>MySQL</li>
    <li>Bootstrap 5</li>
    <li>CKEditor 5</li>
    <li>JWT Authentication</li>
</ul>

<h3>Benefits</h3>
<p>
BookNest improves operational efficiency, simplifies inventory tracking,
enhances user experience, and provides detailed reports for better decision-making.
</p>
--abc
